  "style": {
    "name": "Mughal river-temple — lapis & gold",
    "rationale": "Second pass: deepened the pishtaq to a true 3-block recess with quartz reveals and back wall; broke every flat field with relief — paneled the red plinth, banded the corner pilasters, ran gold string-courses across the bays, and framed the side niches; rebuilt the crown as a belly-overhanging onion dome with converging gold ribs flanked by engaged chhatri kiosks and guldasta corner finials; held the lapis/quartz/gold/terracotta complementary palette and refused the reference's white."
